# Documentation Maintenance

Docs stay truthful or they lie. Update docs in the same session as code changes.

## Decision Matrix

| Change kind | Must update |
|---|---|
| API endpoint added / removed / behavior changed | API docs + README + changelog |
| Database migration (table / index / RLS / function) | Migration file + schema docs + types |
| New env var / renamed env var | `.env.example` + README + changelog |
| Auth flow or permissions changed | Auth docs + README |
| Frontend route or component behavior changed | Frontend README + changelog |
| Dependency bump affecting behavior | README stack section + changelog |
| Architecture or data flow changed | `ARCHITECTURE.md` + changelog |

## Changelog Policy

- Newest entries at the top of changelog files.
- Never append deltas to hub READMEs — hubs stay as stable references.
- If a hub fact is wrong, fix the hub and record the fix in the changelog.

## Verification

Before marking any doc update complete:

- [ ] Every file listed in the decision matrix for the change kind has been updated.
- [ ] Code and docs agree (no stale examples, env vars, or IDs).
- [ ] Changelog delta is present with a date and touchpoints.

## Rationalization Prevention

| Excuse | Reality |
|---|---|
| "The code is self-documenting" | Code does not tell operators how to deploy it. Update the doc. |
| "I'll update docs in a follow-up" | Follow-ups never come. Update in the same commit. |
| "The changelog is noisy" | The changelog is the audit trail. Add the entry. |
